 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Eating out and takeaway food in Melbourne was **3.5% more expensive in August 2026 than in August 2025**.\n\n- **Recent trend:** The annual rise has been between about 3.3% and 4.4% every month since April 2025. It peaked at 4.4% in May 2026 and was 3.9% in June and 4.1% in July.\n- **Compared with the nation:** Australia overall was up 4.1% in the year to August 2026, so Melbourne is running slightly cheaper than the national average.\n- **Compared with 2024:** Prices were rising faster then. Melbourne's annual increase was 5.8% in the March quarter of 2024 and 2.3% in the June quarter of 2025, so inflation in this category has picked up again since mid-2025.\n\nThe category is \"meals out and takeaway foods,\" so it includes restaurant, café and takeaway prices together.",
